  "@id": "https://pices-data.github.io/odis/records/zenodo-23569944.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "South Puget Sound Model Nutrient Study (SPASM)",
  "description": "A 3-Dimensional (3-D) hydrodynamic and water quality model that can be used to evaluate the capacity of South Sound to assimilate waste loads from point and nonpoint sources of nutrients and biochemical oxygen demand (BOD), and meet water quality criteria for dissolved oxygen. Preliminary results are available online at http://www.ecy.wa.gov/programs/eap/spasm/spasm_results.html.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To develop a computer model that can be used to simulate hydrodynamics and water quality, characterize and evaluate pollutant loading, and identify specific point and nonpoint sources of pollutants to South Sound.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23569945",
